# kin/youth/legs/std: the youth's legs in trousers and boots (26 px body; regions: T thigh, K knee, S shin, B boot, O sole)
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, the adult method at the youth's scale (KIN-YOUTH, P2b motion rollout 2026-10-22; docs/MOTION_P2.md
# 3, 7, 12). TWO PARTS, as the adult's: this part is the NEAR leg (and its boot); kin/youth/legs/far (z -1, drawn first) is
# the FAR leg, a whole leg on its own part, a value darker, never narrower (only what the near leg covers hides it). Every
# side walk / run leg is drawn from its joints at the idle's 6 px along the bones (hip > knee band > ankle), 4 px across
# the bone when upright and 5-6 px rows where it angles (THICK 3.8+), ankles 4 px or wider, the first three rows under the
# hem inside the hem span, the far leg's every row at least the near leg's and >= 3 px where it shows beside it. The boot
# is one drawing in its library tilts (boots_youth: Y0 flat, Y1 toe-up, Y2 heel-up, Y3 toe-off, Y9 point), placed by `put`
# (the leg pixels win over 2 px of a boot's heel cap at most). Written by the KIN-YOUTH leg kit (per-frame joint runs,
# shaded: outline on the silhouette, the first interior pixel lit, the knee band's highlight), then traced at 8x.
#   WALK (cycle 18, holds 3 / 3 / 3; plants R 2:-1, -1:-4, -4:-7, L a pixel forward; bob +1 / 0 / 0):
#     contact walkA / walkC: the front leg's thigh down from the hips' front half, the knee over a 5 px shin, Y1 heel
#       strike at +2 (toe up); the back leg upright under the hips' back half, its Y2 up on the toe at -2;
#     pass walkA2 / walkC2: the planted leg straight under the hips (Y0 at -1, the shaft widening to its boot); the swing
#       leg's knee under the seat, the shin back, its Y0 lifted a row behind (heel -6);
#     reach walkB2 / walkD2: the planted leg under the hips' back half (Y0 at -4); the reaching leg's knee forward over a
#       hanging shin, Y1 lifted a row at +2 (it lands there next frame).
#   RUN (cycle 30, holds 5 / 5 / 5; plants R 0:-5, -5:-10, -10:-15, L a pixel forward; bob 0 / -1 / -2; kin_youth.clip
#   leans the upper body 3, the torsos' runl views shear it, the hips ride hip=1):
#     contact run1 / run4: the landing leg flat on Y0 at 0 under a proud knee, the shaft as wide as its boot; the trailing
#       leg down from the seat, the knee under it, the shin down and back (6 px rows) into a flat Y0 lifted behind;
#     push run2 / run5: the support leg one diagonal back from the hips onto its toe (Y3 at 0, 29 deg), the swing thigh
#       driven forward from the hips' front half (6 px rows), the knee out at +5, its Y3 hanging toe down a row up;
#     flight run3 / run6 (both soles 2 rows up): the trailing thigh straight down inside the hips, the knee breaking back,
#       the shin down and back (45 deg) into Y9 pointed; the lead thigh forward (27 deg), the knee up, the shin hanging
#       behind it into a flat Y0 two rows up.
#   The L views: the R pixels mirrored (x' = -x - 1) and re-lit for the top-left light (never the plain mirror). Boy and
#   girl share these drawings (her hips are her garment's: the torsos' run views carry the belt on her hips).
# History (the 2026-10-21 rebuild below is superseded for the side walk and run; front and back keys, the idles and the
# other keys are unchanged):
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, the motion rebuild (2026-10-21; docs/MOTION_P2.md 5.5, STYLE_P2 10 "The owner's motion reference"):
# every side (R, L) walk and run key is two continuous limbs at the youth's own scale, hip > thigh (F-7, F-6) > knee (F-5,
# the last trouser row) > shin (the boot shaft) > foot, in a scissor stride. In the side walk and run the youth's hangs
# (kin/youth/wear/*_hang wide / flare) end a row higher (the tunic a lone hem row at F-8), so the seat row F-7 SHOWS: three
# trouser rows, the legs parting from the crotch on F-6 at contact (motion fix round 3, R3-06: "boots shuffling under the
# hem"). The foot is ONE boot in five hand-drawn tilts of the youth's idle foot (maps/stamps/boots_youth.stamps: Y0 flat,
# Y1 toe-up, Y2 heel-up, Y3 toe-off, Y4 pointed; near and far; R and L re-lit), never sheared, squashed or tool-rotated,
# placed by `put` (the ground pivot: the heel of Y0 / Y1, the toe of Y2 / Y3 / Y4). Plants = the planted heel (kin_youth.clip).
#   Walk (cycle 16; plants 2:-1, -1:-4, -4:-6): contact walkA / walkC, the front Y1 landing on its heel at +2, toe up two
#   rows, its shin's F-4 row running into the toe cap (fix round 3: the instep closed, no notch), the back Y2 up on its
#   toe pad at -1, the heel two rows up, its shin's last row on the key's top beside the heel; down walkA2 / walkC2 (bob 1,
#   the hem down with the body), the front Y0 planted at -1 under a flexed knee (the kneecap a pixel forward on F-5), the
#   back Y3 rolled onto its toe at -3 (registered); pass walkB2 / walkD2 (fix round 3), the planted Y0 at -4 straight under
#   the hips (a 4 px column), the swing leg's knee driven forward (F-6, u 0..+5) over a 4 px shin, its Y3 toe down AHEAD of
#   the planted toe (toe +6, lifted 1): the two boots apart by daylight (BOOTSPLIT), the swing boot whole.
#   Run (cycle 30; plants 2:-3, -3:-7, -7:-13; every visible trouser pixel the knee region): contact run1 / run4, a flat Y0
#   landing at +2 under a bent knee, the trailing leg down and back from the hip, its knee at F-6 and a 3 px shin stepping
#   back onto the Y3 hung toe down behind (toe -2, lifted 1: the ankle about 110 degrees); push run2 / run5, the planted leg
#   under the hips (Y0 at -3), the swing knee driving forward with its Y3 folded under it, toe down and lifted 2, clear of
#   the planted boot (toe +6); flight run3 / run6 (bob -1), the leading knee up (F-7) over a hanging shin and a Y0 lifted 2
#   at +2, the trailing knee bent, its Y3 pointed (toe -2, lifted 2). The left views: the right views mirrored
#   (x' = -x - 1), every band re-lit for the top-left light. `when girl replace` side views: the boy's placements, her back
#   hip a pixel fuller on the seat and first visible rows.
# History (superseded for the side walk and run by the rebuild above; front and back keys, the idles and the other
# keys are unchanged):
# kin/youth/legs/std: the youth's legs in trousers and boots (26 px body; regions: T thigh, K knee, S shin, B boot, O sole)
# KIN-YOUTH (P2b wave 2). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. The adult's rules at the youth's size (STYLE_P2 3, 10): two chunky
# trouser legs (5 px each, the crotch a shared seam) over the idle boot (a 5 px shaft, a 6 px toe, flat on the sole row);
# every walk and run frame is the idle's boots moved and lifted, never drawn at an angle; the legs are upright trouser
# blocks that step a pixel at the knee and at the hip. Front and back: the landing and the swing foot lifted 1 (the hem
# holds still over the down frames, so the visible mass stays 90 % or more of the idle's), the run's flight the idle
# lifted 1. Side views: contact walkA / walkC (both soles flat, 6 px apart), down walkA2 / walkC2 (the planted knee a
# pixel forward, the trailing boot lifted 1), pass walkB2 / walkD2 (the planted leg under the hips, the swing boot lifted
# 2 ahead); the soles step 3 / 3 / 2 px on kin_youth.clip's plants. The left views are the right views' shapes mirrored,
# each run re-lit from the left. `buckle` the knees giving way (the fall), `lie` the legs together, toes up (lying).
# No stretch row: the doll lifts an elf's whole body a pixel (doll_compose) and the youth's frame stays 26 (art_rig.h).
# The side run, round 4 (2026-10-20, with the adult's: the owner saw the feet "completely disconnected from the body")
# joined each boot to a trouser stub; round 5 (the leg pass, 2026-10-20) redrew every side run leg as a limb: each
# boot under its own trouser with both of the youth's trouser rows (F-6, F-5) showing between the hem (F-7) and the
# boot top: no boot is lifted against the hem but the passing one (lifted 1 beside the planted leg). Contact run1 /
# run4: both boots down, 13 px across with a pixel of air between them (the planted sole +2..+7: kin_youth.clip's run
# plants 5 / 4 / 6), the back heel at -5; the reaching leg angled a pixel a row from the hip. Push run2 / run5: the
# planted leg straight under the hips, the swing boot lifted 1 beside it. Flight run3 / run6 (bob -1): both boots a
# pixel off the ground, the pushing leg trailing on a diagonal, the leading leg reaching, a pixel of air between them.
# Made from the right view's leg placements (thigh start per row, shaft start, lift); the left views mirror them a
# pixel forward, re-lit from the left.
use person
body youth
role legs std
layer legs
anchor pivot
keys legs
stamps boots_youth
tags boots-stamped

